  "summary": "Yumen Pass, the Jade Gate, was a Han frontier gate west of Dunhuang that controlled the road to the Western Regions. Dunhuang commandery was set up in 111 BCE, and wooden documents from the pass date largely to the 90s BCE. It is now a Silk Roads World Heritage component.",
